      "claim": "The spec declares `risk: standard`, but its `touches` list includes `saffron/ledger.py`, which is in this repo's `elevate_on` set (`.saffron/policy.yaml`). Per the repo's own convention, touching an `elevate_on` path auto-elevates the effective risk tier regardless of the declared `risk:` field, making the `size` gate blocking rather than advisory. The spec's own Notes section already states this correctly and the cited prototype measurement (1630 changed tokens) stays under the `feature` ceiling of 3000 either way, so no change is needed, but the bare frontmatter `risk: standard` is misleading read on its own and this is exactly the gate condition worth a reviewer's explicit confirmation before the cell starts.",
